# Influencer's Weekend Drive - Writeup

First of all, uploading the .png file on Google Lens, the car name shows up to be 'Range Rover Sport'.

Then scrolling down below according to the image given, it can be seen that the content creator comes out to be 'Faisal Khan'.

Now comes the trickiest part, finding the co-ordinates of the location where the image was taken.

We uploaded the image of three buildings on the Google Lens and the result came out to be 'Keshav Kunj 4 Apartments' in Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra.
Most of the participants might enter the co-ordinates of the Palm Beach Road but that's where they go wrong.
Using more techniques and searching for a look-a-like location as in the YouTube video, we found a path that led to a popular landmark, a park named 'Flamingo Bird Watch' on the Google Maps.
Now throughout that path or road, we step-by-step checked for the angle and point that fits almost perfectly while capturing the shot.
So here we got the co-ordinates (not exact, but almost correct that's why I asked for the co-ordinates upto 3 decimal places only).
The co-ordinates are: 19.010, 73.009 (latitude, longitude) and the location is: Sector 58A, Seawoods, Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706

So, finally the flag comes out to be: flag{rangeroversport + faisalkhan + 19.010,73.009}.
